From: Benedek Kupper <kupper.benedek@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: udc: nrf: leave low power when enabled

The USBD keeps LOWPOWER while it is disabled, unless it stays disabled
long enough. When the stack disables the controller while the bus is
suspended (the peripheral is in low power), and enables it again right
away, the peripheral starts in low power. As it did not suspend since it
was enabled, bus activity does not wake it: the host's reset is still
reported, but the device does not answer any transaction, until a host
resume, which a host does not send to a device it just reset.

Write ForceNormal when enabling the peripheral: it is not suspended yet.

Seen on nRF52840 with a soft detach and attach back to back while the
bus was suspended (4 of 5 attempts); with a 1 ms gap, or on an active
bus, the device recovered.
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/udc/udc_nrf.c b/drivers/usb/udc/udc_nrf.c
index bb7d4d2f968..50417eaab7d 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/udc/udc_nrf.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/udc/udc_nrf.c
@@ -838,6 +838,7 @@ static void nrf_usbd_legacy_enable(void)
 	NRF_USBD->EVENTCAUSE = USBD_EVENTCAUSE_READY_Msk;
 
 	nrf_usbd_peripheral_enable();
+	NRF_USBD->LOWPOWER = USBD_LOWPOWER_LOWPOWER_ForceNormal << USBD_LOWPOWER_LOWPOWER_Pos;
 
 	if (nrf_usbd_common_errata_223() && m_first_enable) {
 		NRF_USBD->ENABLE = 0;
